{
  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that multiprofile with scvi_n200 and avgpool (config_002, acc 0.650) dramatically outperforms singleprofile RNA-only (config_009, acc 0.520), while adding resnet50 image in the singleprofile setting (config_014) yields only a marginal +0.016 gain. The key uncertainty is whether image contributes meaningfully when combined with the multiprofile gain. config_037 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is the minimal extension of config_002: it adds the same resnet50 image encoder and concat fusion already validated in config_014, while keeping aggregation (avgpool) and RNA encoder (scvi_n200) identical. This isolates the image contribution in the multiprofile regime. If it matches or beats 0.650, image is worth retaining; if not, we can focus remaining budget on RNA-only multiprofile refinements (e.g., aggregation method or encoder choice) without the added complexity of a second modality."
}

